@startuml j6-shared-tickets
!include c4-sequence.iuml
title J6 Shared tickets and the desk code
actor "Staff" as Staff <<person>>
box "In the staff browser"
participant "Staff page\n(staff/staff.js,\nsync.js)" as SP <<container>>
end box
box "Vercel functions"
participant "api/health.js" as Health <<container>>
participant "api/tickets.js" as Tix <<container>>
end box
database "Postgres\n(Neon)" as Store <<store>>
box "In the patient's browser"
participant "Patient chat on\nanother device\n(chat.js, sync.js)" as Chat <<container>>
end box
actor "Patient" as Patient <<person>>

== Opening the staff page ==
Staff -> SP : opens /staff
SP -> Health : sync.js: GET /api/health\n(no desk code typed yet)
alt the store is reachable
  Health --> SP : the store is "postgres"
else the store cannot be reached
  note over SP, Health : the page says so and shows\nthe tickets kept in this browser
end
SP --> Staff : this browser's tickets, and\n"Enter the desk code to see\ntickets from every device."
note over SP, Staff : without the desk code the staff page\nshows this browser's tickets only
== The desk code ==
Staff -> SP : types the desk code\nand presses "Use code"
SP -> Tix : sync.js: GET /api/tickets\n(with the desk code)
Tix -> Tix : compares it with\nFRONTDESK_DESK_CODE
alt the code matches
  Tix -> Store : read the newest tickets\nof every device
  Tix --> SP : the list
  SP --> Staff : "<n> from other devices";\nthe queue shows them,\nurgent first
else wrong code (401), or none set on the server (403)
  note over SP, Tix : the page asks for the code again,\nor says the clinic has not set one
end
== A new ticket from a phone ==
Patient -> Chat : asks a question\non a phone
Chat -> Tix : sync.js: POST /api/tickets\n(the ticket, with\nthat browser's key)
Tix -> Store : a row in the table tickets,\nowned by the hash of the key
loop every 5 s while the page is open
  SP -> Tix : sync.js: GET /api/tickets again,\nabout every five seconds
  Tix --> SP : the list, now with\nthe new ticket
end
SP --> Staff : the new ticket\nappears in the queue
@enduml
